Remove the transmit tail-pointer reader after the engineering procfs and
sysfs callers have been removed.  Keeping the now-unreferenced helper adds a
W=1 warning and leaves unnecessary direct register-access code in production
builds.

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8126/r8126_n.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8126/r8126_n.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8126/r8126_n.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8126/r8126_n.c
@@ -672,26 +672,6 @@ rtl8126_get_hw_clo_ptr(struct rtl8126_tx_ring *ring)
         }
 }
 
